# coverage.map -- which source paths each suite reads. tools/nx/suites.js turns each line into the
# inputs of the suite's Nx target, so editing a path re-runs every suite that reads it and replays
# the others from Nx's cache; that file's header has the rules in full.
#
# Line forms (a keyword or a suite file name, then globs; a word may repeat on several lines):
#   <suite file>  <glob>...   the suite READS these paths: an edit to one re-runs the suite
#   tree <suite>  <glob>...   a whole-tree check: an edit to a match re-runs it, but it claims
#                             nothing, so it can never be what makes a path count as covered
#   core          <glob>...   the shared core: an edit to one re-runs EVERY suite
#   exempt        <glob>...   shipped, and read by no suite on purpose; an edit re-runs no suite of
#                             its own (a tree check that matches still runs)
#   refs <suite>  <glob>...   the suite NAMES these paths without reading them (fixture text), so
#                             the literal-reference check below does not require a claim
# Globs: `*` is any run of characters but `/`, `**` any run including `/`, `?` one character but `/`.
#
# A path no line claims re-runs nothing when it changes, so it is refused: `node tools/nx/suites.js
# --check` (run by test-coverage-map.py) refuses a tracked file nothing claims or exempts and a suite
# that names a tracked path it does not claim. The plugin itself refuses, failing every Nx command, a
# suite with no line here, a line naming no suite, a line with no globs and a glob that matches no
# tracked file. A suite file claims itself; it needs no line for that.

# --- the shared core: what every suite runs through -------------------------------------------
core tests/git-isolate.sh tests/git-isolated.gitconfig
core dot_gitconfig
core private_dot_local/bin/executable_install-test-gate private_dot_local/bin/executable_git-staged-run
core run_onchange_install-git-hooks.sh.tmpl

